- /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/schc/src/compress.rs lines 52-83

## Problem
```rust
pub struct FieldDescriptor {
    pub field_id: &'static str,
    // ...
    pub mapping: Option<&'static [u128]>,
}

pub struct Rule {
    // ...
    pub fields: &'static [FieldDescriptor],
}
```

All references are `'static`, meaning rules must be compile-time constants. Users cannot construct rules dynamically at runtime (e.g., from configuration files, network negotiation, or user input) without using `Box::leak` or similar memory leaks.

## API Risk
This forces a specific usage pattern and limits integration with systems that need runtime-defined compression contexts.

## Suggested Fix
Make the types generic over lifetime:
```rust
pub struct FieldDescriptor<'a> {
    pub field_id: &'a str,
    pub mapping: Option<&'a [u128]>,
}
pub struct Rule<'a> {
    pub fields: &'a [FieldDescriptor<'a>],
}
```

